@startuml

title Updating a job definition: the write, the version, and the loop's re-read

actor "the caller" as caller
participant "the scheduler service" as service
database "the job definitions table" as table
participant "the loop" as loop

caller -> service : put the definition\n(the fields, a change reason,\na precondition on the version it read)
service -> table : close the current row;\ninsert the next version
table --> service : the stored definition,\nwith its new version
service --> caller : the stored definition

table --> loop : the change event\n(created, updated or deleted)
loop -> loop : re-read the job set,\nand re-arm the timer

note over loop
    The loop does not poll the table.
    Any change event re-reads the set and
    re-arms the sleep.
end note

... the next due instant ...

loop -> loop : fire each definition whose occurrence has arrived
loop -> loop : recompute that definition's next occurrence

note over service, loop
    A firing already in flight keeps the definition
    the loop read; the change applies to later firings.
end note

@enduml
